# rules: kotlin-archive-entry-path-not-checked
# languages: kotlin
# fixture: kotlin/CWE-22-archive.kt
# from: CWE-22 (Path Traversal), the Zip Slip family
#
# A zip entry's name is a path chosen by whoever built the archive, and nothing
# in the format forbids `../`. So `File(target, entry.name)` resolves outside
# the directory the extraction was meant to stay in, and on Android that is the
# app's own data directory: an update archive that overwrites
# `shared_prefs/auth.xml`, or drops a .dex where the app will load it.
#
# The source is a receiver *named* like an entry rather than any `.name`. This
# is the narrowing the C# pass had to learn and the reason is the same: `.name`
# belongs to File and to a dozen other types, and reading it off all of them
# reported `Path.Combine(target.FullName, fi.Name)` in an ordinary recursive
# copy. A receiver called `entry`, `zipEntry`, `ze` or `e` inside a loop over
# entries is what an extraction looks like, and it is cheap.
#
# The check that makes this safe is a comparison - resolve the destination,
# confirm it still starts with the target - and a comparison is not a call this
# rule can see. So the exclusion is the method's own text: a method that
# mentions `canonicalPath` or `startsWith` beside its extraction is a method
# somebody has already thought about, and it is left alone as a whole. That is
# coarser than a structural test, it costs a method that checks one path and
# extracts another unchecked, and quiet is the right direction to be coarse in.

["File($D, $N)", "File($D, $N).$M()", "Paths.get($D, $N)",
 "FileOutputStream($D, $N)", "$D.resolve($N)"] as $destinations
| ["fun $F($$$_) { $BODY }"] as $methods
| "^(?:entry|zipEntry|ze|e|tarEntry|jarEntry)\\." as $anEntry
| "canonicalPath|canonicalFile|startsWith|normalize" as $alreadyChecked
| scan_ast("*.kt"; $destinations + $methods) as $all
| ( $all | of($destinations)
    | where_capture("N"; $anEntry)
    | where_capture("N"; "\\.name$|\\.getName\\(\\)$")
    | outside($all | of($methods) | where_capture("BODY"; $alreadyChecked)) )
| finding("kotlin-archive-entry-path-not-checked";
    "$N is a path out of the archive, so an entry called ../../shared_prefs/x "
    + "is written outside the directory this was extracting into")
| report
